    "result_text": "The build succeeds and all tests pass. Here's a summary of what I implemented:\n\n## Change\n\nOn successful owner creation, a welcome notification is now enqueued via a logger named `NOTIFY`, carrying the owner id and memberId.\n\n## Implementation\n\n**New component** \u2014 `rest/notification/WelcomeNotifier.java`:\n- A `@Component` with a single responsibility: emit the welcome notification to the dedicated `NOTIFY` logger. Its `enqueueWelcome(Owner)` method logs a line containing `ownerId` and `memberId`.\n- Placed in its own `notification` package, mirroring the existing `rest/audit/OwnerAuditLogger` pattern \u2014 keeping notification dispatch decoupled from the audit trail rather than overloading the audit logger.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n- Injected `WelcomeNotifier` via the constructor (added field + parameter + assignment).\n- Called `this.welcomeNotifier.enqueueWelcome(owner)` in `createOwner(...)`, right after the audit log, so it fires only on a successful create (after persistence, and not on idempotency-key replays).\n\nThe new acceptance test `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` passes \u2014 the captured `NOTIFY` output confirms the line carries both the id and memberId:\n\n```\nINFO  NOTIFY - Welcome notification enqueued: ownerId=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1\n```\n\n`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests green.",
